(1. PURPOSE OF MILITARY GRID SYSTEM: The Purple Grid network drawn across) Tj
T*
(survey maps enables troops to designate any point on earth accurately) Tj
T*
(without relying on complex geographical latitude and longitude coordinates.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. EASTINGS & NORTHINGS: Eastings are the vertical grid lines numbered) Tj
T*
(sequentially from West to East \(left to right\). Northings are the) Tj
T*
(horizontal grid lines numbered sequentially from South to North \(bottom to) Tj
T*
(top\). The fundamental reading rule is: "Along the corridor first) Tj
T*
(\(Eastings\), then up the stairs \(Northings\)".) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. 4-FIGURE GRID REFERENCE: Identifies a 1 square kilometer grid box.) Tj
T*
(Example: Easting line 42 and Northing line 68 yield the 4-figure reference) Tj
T*
(GR 4268.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. 6-FIGURE GRID REFERENCE DECOMPOSITION: Divides each 1 km grid square) Tj
T*
(into tenths \(100-meter precision\). To locate a bunker at 3 tenths east of) Tj
T*
(line 42 and 7 tenths north of line 68, the full 6-figure reference is) Tj
T*
(written as GR 423687 \(Easting 42 + 3, Northing 68 + 7\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
